INFO 7823 :: Page 165 :: 7.30 pm Fort Monroe Mch 14th 1865 7 pm for Secy Navy ---- Monitor Lehigh in from Charleston and will go up the James river immy ---- No news of the Montauk ---- our troops in possession of Kinston NC Glissen Capt Senior officer 8.20 P. M City Pt Mar. 14th 1865 7. PM 14th To Gen. C. Hoffman ---- My dispatch to the Secy of War applied to prisoners of war ---- Continuous reports of men being retained in irons are being brought by prisoners going forward for exchange ---- I made a proposition applying to citizens but received no reply ---- There is I believe a large number of prisoners in irons at Alton Illinois who have been sentenced by Military commissions who should be released under the agreement made ---- U. S. Grant Lt Genl 940 PM Chattanooga pm 1865 - 8pm PM S. H. Beckwith Chattanooga Mar. 14th 1865 8 PM Chattanooga 5 P. M. 14th for Gen Grant ---- Genl Stoneman has not started yet. I am now on my way to Knoxville to get him off. The heavy rains have delayed him up to this time ---- One Division of Infantry is now on its way to Bulls Gap. The others will follow as we get the transportation sig Geo H. Thomas Maj Genl
INFO 7825 :: Page 167 :: Recd 18th 6 P. M. New Orleans La mar 10. 1865 New Orleans Mar. 10th Gen Grant City Pt Va ---- Gen Canby left here March 5th for Mobile bay where Grangers Command & A. J. Smith's command now are with the exception of two or 3 thousand men who are now getting off ---- Steele with about 8,000 men is at Pens - a = = cola probably to move on Blakely ---- Grierson is here & his cavalry coming ---- He goes I am told to Gen Canby & it will take him a week to get his Command there ---- much delay has been caused by a Cipher clerks blunder which made <insertion>A.<insertion> J. Smith land at Vicksburg & discharge his steam boats ---- Rebels supposed to have nine thousand men at Mobile & as many at Blakely signed C. B. Comstock Bt. Br. Genl.
INFO 8642 :: Page 164 :: 9 am 14th Mar 1865 Laurel Hill N C Wednesday Mch 8th ---- 18 65 for Comdg officer Wilmington we are marching on Fayetteville will be there Saturday Sunday and Monday and then will march for Goldsboro . if possible send a boat up Cape fear river and have word conveyed to Schofield that I expect to meet him about Goldsboro . we are all well and have done finely . The rain makes our roads difficult and may delay me about Fayetteville in which case I would like to have some bread sugar and coffee we have an abundance of all else . I expect to reach Goldsboro by the 20th instant WT Sherman Maj Genl
INFO 8644 :: Page 166 :: 430 P. M City Pt Mar. 14th 1865 4.30 P. M City Point Mar. 14th 1865 14th 3 PM for Secy War I am very much dissatisfied with Gen Canby ---- he has been slow beyond excuse . I wrote to him long since that he could not trust Granger in command , after that he nominated him for the Command of a Corps ---- I wrote to him too that he must command the troops going into the field in person ---- on the 1st of march he is in New Orleans & does not say a word about leaving there ---- I would like now to have Steele , as I recommended long since in a dispatch ad - dressed to Gen. Halbeck , put in command of the 13th Corps ---- assoonas Sheridan can be spared I will want him to supercede Canby & the latter put in command of the Dept of Gulf unless he does far better in the next few weeks than I now have any reason to hope for ---- US Grant LtGen
